# ActaLog Frontend (Vue.js) Environment Configuration
# ============================================================================
# PURPOSE: Configuration for the Vue.js frontend build process
# USAGE:   Copy to .env in the web/ directory (only if needed)
#
# OTHER .env FILES IN THIS PROJECT:
#   - /.env.example (project root) -> Backend server configuration
#                                     Required for running the Go backend
#   - /docker/.env.example         -> Docker deployment configuration
#                                     Use when running with docker-compose
#
# NOTE: This file is usually NOT needed because:
#   - In development: Vite proxy forwards /api requests to the backend
#   - In production:  The Go server serves both API and frontend on port 8080
#
# Only create web/.env if your frontend needs to connect to an API server
# running on a different domain or port (e.g., separate frontend hosting).
# ============================================================================
#
# Vite Environment Variables

# API Base URL (optional)
# In development: leave empty to use Vite proxy (default behavior)
# In production: set to your backend API URL if on a different domain/port
# Examples:
#   - Same domain, different port: http://your-domain.com:8080
#   - Different domain: https://api.your-domain.com
#   - Local IP: http://192.168.1.100:8080
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=

# Note: All environment variables must start with VITE_ to be exposed to the client
# See: https://vitejs.dev/guide/env-and-mode.html
